Description: Linux: use cpu_feature_enabled() instead of static_cpu_has()
 static_cpu_has() was hidden and renamed to _static_cpu_has() in Linux 7.3
 (kernel commit 3eaa50e1e255 "x86/cpu: Hide and rename static_cpu_has()").
 Since 3.18 cpu_feature_enabled() has been the right way to do the same
 thing unconditionally, so switch everything over.
 .
 Rebased onto 2.4.4, where simd_stat.c still tests the HAVE_* macros
 directly rather than through the HAVE_SIMD() helper introduced upstream.
Author: Rob Norris <robn@despairlabs.com>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/robn/zfs/commit/cc99b331dae08e59fa16909ceea8526aa82f4a5e
Forwarded: not-needed
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
